kai: Ran the quickstart and saw two problems together: 1) warmup prefetch spawns 20 embed+gen calls, 2) our auth refresh path races and sometimes replays a warmup request. result: duplicated load + 429s on first-run.

rachel: can you paste a tiny trace? Hosted or Dedicated?

kai: Hosted. trace excerpt: 
```
[2024-11-02T06:12:01Z] INFO req=aa1 status=401 auth=expired
[2024-11-02T06:12:01Z] DEBUG auth refresh start token=tmp123
[2024-11-02T06:12:01Z] INFO req=aa1 retry-after-401 replay idempotency=missing
[2024-11-02T06:12:02Z] WARN req=bb2 status=429 inflight=42
```

diego: that explains it. two orthogonal bugs: (A) aggressive prefetch/prefill defaults in the sampleapps, (B) refresh logic that doesn't gate concurrent refreshes or attach idempotency keys for warmup calls. fix ideas: cap prefill to 6 for hosted, add singleflight auth refresh (or a promise cache in SDK), and add optional idempotency header for non-user requests (X-Idempotency-Key).

rachel: agree. also let's change pagination quickstart: show a streaming iterator example and a limited prefetch=1 variant. many teams assume prefetch=all is fine and then hit backpressure.

kai: proposed JS helper to attach idempotency + safe warmup (short):
```js
async function safeWarmup(client, items, {maxInflight=6}={}){
  const sem = new Semaphore(maxInflight);
  await Promise.all(items.map(async (it)=>{ await sem.acquire();
    try {
      await client.request(it, {headers:{'X-Idempotency-Key': generateKey(it)}});
    } finally { sem.release(); }
  }))
}
```

diego: for SDK parity: add singleflight auth for Python/Go/JS and expose a config flag `auth.singleflight=true` defaulting to true. also standardize sampleapp defaults in quickstart repo. I'll open issues for Py/Go.

ci-bot: created pipeline `quickstart/safe-warmup` on branch `devex/safe-warmup` and queued concurrency smoke test.

rachel: action items: 1) quick change to sampleapp defaults (prefill=6, maxInflight=6), 2) SDK singleflight auth + idempotency helper, 3) docs update with streaming pagination and warmup anti-patterns. i'll take docs + quickstart PR.

kai: thanks — will run a staging onboarding after PR and paste results here.
